**Why Scripture was slower than The Table** — in [ReferencePane.qml](qml/components/ReferencePane.qml) both tabs staged a pick, but the two branches paid for the chapter's slide set in a different order:

- **The Table**: staged the one picked slide, then built the chapter set (170 paragraphs for your current sermon — see [engine.log](build/logs/engine.log) `SlideWarm` "remaining 122 paragraph(s) cut in 46 ms"). The tile updated *before* that work, so it felt instant.
- **Scripture**: called `chapterOutputSlides()` **first** — one engine slide build per verse (31 for Genesis 1, each composed through the template) — and then handed that whole 31-slide set to `stageSlideSet`. So the tile waited on all of it before showing anything, and the set it staged was 31 slides for a click that shows one. That's the asymmetry you noticed: Bible is lighter than The Table and still drew later.

**What changed** ([ReferencePane.qml](qml/components/ReferencePane.qml)):

- Both pick branches now stage **one** slide, immediately. `rememberPick(null, …)` remembers the pick by *piece*, not by a pre-built slide set.
- The chapter set that Slide mode needs for its step neighbours is filled by `fillPickSet()` on a **zero-delay timer**, so the tile is updated and painted before it runs. Scroll mode skips it entirely — its walk reads the page list anyway.
- Scroll-off (`applyScrollMode`) builds the set only when it is actually wanted, and now finds the pick's own slide in a freshly built set instead of assuming a remembered index.

**Measured**

- The engine's own log puts the removed work at **78 ms for Genesis 1** ("cut the first 31 item(s) ahead of the click in 78 ms") — and that is only the cut, before the 31 slides were converted, copied and staged on the interface thread. All of it sat in front of the tile update.
- I added a `[PICKCOST]` probe to the click path: it logs `[PICKCOST] scripture 12 staged in N ms (scroll|slide)` whenever a pick takes ≥ 80 ms. In this session so far it has logged **nothing** (`grep -c PICKCOST` → 0) across a Table pick served warm with no interface-thread fill.
- `tools/dev_cycle.sh --build-only` → `build OK / DEV_CYCLE: PASS`; relaunched, health OK, and the boot log for this run (18:23) has no QML/JS errors.

**What to check**: open Scripture and double-click a verse — the tile should now show it as promptly as The Table does. If it still lags, don't guess: that `[PICKCOST]` line will name the exact milliseconds and the mode, and it means the remaining cost is past this path (which we can then chase with a number instead of a theory).

One behaviour gap I want to name rather than hide: in Slide mode a step press now finds its neighbours a tick after the click instead of instantly — that's the deferred `fillPickSet()`. In practice it lands long before you can press ‹ ›, but it is the one thing that was technically instant before.

The other uncommitted files in `git diff --stat` (`Main.qml`, `ShowCenter.qml`, `GeneralScreen.qml`, `AppSettings.cpp`) are from earlier work in this session and untouched by this change.
