**[RoutingNodeCard.qml](qml/components/RoutingNodeCard.qml)** and **[RoutingPort.qml](qml/components/RoutingPort.qml)** are the two pieces: the card is pure presentation (title, subtitle, state, signal pill, style swatch, hover reporting) and the port is a bare 9px dot with a 25px grab area reporting its drag in scene coordinates.

**[RoutingDraft.qml](qml/settings/RoutingDraft.qml)** holds the wires for the session, so leaving Routing for Outputs and coming back does not wipe the canvas. Wires are keyed by **identity, not position** — a bus's stable id, a style's id, a screen's name (all OutputListModel has, and `uniqueOutputName` guarantees it) — so deleting a bus can't silently re-point every wire below it, and pruning is skipped while a model is momentarily empty (a restore/reset) so a reset can't delete the graph. Seeding is coalesced behind `EngineBridge.booted` so the canvas never seeds from half-loaded rosters: it wires each screen to the style Outputs already gives it, the first video bus into every screen, that bus's audio into Speakers/Icecast/Recording, and each screen into the sink its kind names.

