Done. The graph no longer filters edges by an output's declared signal type, so an audio bus can actually reach an NDI, recording or streaming row.

## The change

[ProductionGraph.cpp](src/PresentationEngine/modules/production/ProductionGraph.cpp):

- `Accepts()` now treats an `Output` node as a **signal sink**: it terminates whatever reaches it. What a row may carry stays its `OutputConfig` caps (a physical screen is video-only), enforced in `AssignOutputBuses` — where the refusal can name the row instead of looking like a dead drag.
- `CanConnect()` asks the same `Accepts()` instead of comparing `signalType` by hand, so the canvas's optimistic drop gate and `Connect()` can no longer disagree (they already disagreed for Data/Control sinks before this).

Why it was needed end to end: a row's node is created as a `Video` node (that's its picture), so the audio edge was refused. The wire still appeared — the canvas draws it from the `OutputConfig` that `RoutingService` writes — but nothing consumed it, because `AudioMixer::MixSelected` resolves an output's feeds through the **edge set**, and a recording taps the mix of *its own* output node. So "audio wired to NDI" drew a wire and sent silence. Both facts are now written by one gesture: the config for persistence/validation, the edge for the engine.

## Test

[TestProductionOutputSignalEdges](src/PresentationEngine/tests/unit/tests_production.cpp) — registered as `production/output-signals`:

- `CanConnect` and `Connect` both accept video **and** audio into a node created as `Video`.
- `Validate()` reports no `signal_mismatch` for a both-signal sink.
- A video-only row still refuses audio **at the caps**.
- The behaviour, not the bookkeeping: a media row's audio, wired only through that edge, reaches a `MixTap` attached to `out:ndi` (`tapsHeard == 1`, `peak > 0.5`) — with no speaker wiring at all. Cutting the edge silences the tap.

## Checks run

- `production/output-signals`: **20 checks, 0 failures**, exit 0.
- Both changed translation units compile (`ProductionGraph.cpp.obj`, `tests_production.cpp.obj`) and `libengine_core.a` + `bps_unit_tests.exe` link. The three build guards ran on the way: `SETTINGS_KEYS: PASS`, `0 new HARD` gui-thread findings, lock-scope `clean (409 files)`.

## One thing I did not touch

The full `production` phase has **6 pre-existing failures** that are not from this change: `audio-mixer` lines 727–732 and `audio-dsp` line 1007. `AudioMixer.cpp` is modified in the working tree by the engine work in flight, and that block expects `Render()` to return true with **no** speaker edge — which the new `kSpeakersOutputId` contract forbids. That test block also carries 4 other uncommitted hunks from that work, so I left its assertions alone rather than paper over what is being rewritten.

Files I changed: [ProductionGraph.cpp](src/PresentationEngine/modules/production/ProductionGraph.cpp), [tests_production.cpp](src/PresentationEngine/tests/unit/tests_production.cpp), [TestDecls.hpp](src/PresentationEngine/tests/unit/TestDecls.hpp), [main.cpp](src/PresentationEngine/tests/unit/main.cpp), and [RoutingService.cpp](qml/services/RoutingService.cpp) (its comment now states the real rule instead of the old limitation).
