Facts I know from this session:
1. Bus → output audio: `RoutingService::assignBus(row,"audio",bus)` writes `AssignOutputBuses` (config, validated for caps) AND `graph.Connect(busNode, outNode, SignalType::Audio)` — the edge set the mixer reads.
2. AudioMixer sums planes whose id == target or whose edge reaches target (`MixInto`/`MixSelected`), and per-target mix taps exist: `AudioEngine::AddMixTap(outputNodeId, MixTap)`; RecordingEngine registers a tap (RecordingEngine.cpp:1528) keyed by an output node id, so a wired audio bus reaches the recording/stream tap.
3. Speaker endpoint `out:speakers` is created by `AudioEngine::EnsureSpeakersOutput` with caps the mixer needs; the canvas wires buses into it via edges (additive, `unwireBus` names the bus).
4. Per-side trim (L/R): `ChannelPill` in the canvas calls `BusListModel.channelGain` / `toggleChannelGain` — engine-side gain per channel (verified functions exist).
5. Levels: `busChannelMix` reads AudioInputListModel levels (engine meters).

