**Why the reverse drag failed**

It wasn't the gesture — dragging output → bus uses the same symmetric code as bus → output: [pairOk](qml/screens/settings/RoutingScreen.qml#L1112) normalises the two ends left-to-right by column, and [toggleWire](qml/screens/settings/RoutingScreen.qml#L1215) reads `fromKey`/`toKey` from that normalisation, so direction never enters the pairing. Your screenshot proves the drag *did* reach the engine: that toast is `ProductionGraph`'s own error string, `output out:out-1 does not accept audio`, surfaced by `RoutingService::assignBus`.

The gate was the **stored caps on your existing HDMI node**. `CapsFor` (the canvas side) had started reporting audio, so the canvas offered the wire — but the node in the saved graph was created by an older build with `supportsAudio: false`, and `AssignOutputBuses` refused against *that*. So the audio half died at assignment no matter which end you dragged from; the video half always worked.

