- [ProductionGraph.cpp:627](src/PresentationEngine/modules/production/ProductionGraph.cpp#L627) — `AssignOutputBuses` no longer asks the node's caps for the audio side: an output is a transport, and every transport takes audio. Video stays gated by caps (the speaker endpoint still refuses video). This also makes a graph saved by an older build behave, instead of needing a migration of the stored `supportsAudio:false`.
- [ProductionGraph.cpp:958](src/PresentationEngine/modules/production/ProductionGraph.cpp#L958) — `Validate()` no longer flags "assigned audio but does not accept audio", for the same stale-document reason.
- [RoutingService.cpp:61](qml/services/RoutingService.cpp#L61) — `CapsFor` gives every transport both signals (HDMI included), and [acceptsSignal](qml/services/RoutingService.cpp#L450) now answers from that one table instead of a separate `IsScreenKind` rule, so a row can't be draggable on the canvas and refused three calls down.
