Both sides now hold sets, with the wires as the allow-list.

**An output carries several buses per side**

The split is now explicit: the graph's **edges** are what is wired (a set, per side), and `OutputConfig` keeps the one-per-side facts — `videoBusId` is which of them is on air, `audioBusId` the first. [refresh()](qml/services/RoutingService.cpp#L627) walks every output node's upstream buses once and publishes both sets (`videoBuses`, `audioBuses`), so the canvas draws a wire per bus instead of one per side. It also re-points the config whenever the bus it names is no longer wired, so an output can never keep naming a bus somebody unplugged — unplug the one being shown and it falls to the first wire still there.

**Wiring adds, unwiring takes one away**

[assignBus](qml/services/RoutingService.cpp#L746) no longer disconnects the previous bus: it adds the edge and leaves the on-air bus alone (the config is only written when that side had none, so the first wire becomes the shown one). `-1` still means "clear this whole side", which is what the card menus' "Unwire video/audio" use. [unwireBus](qml/services/RoutingService.cpp#L891) now applies to every row, not just the speakers: it removes exactly the bus named and hands the config to another wired bus if it was the one named.

**The click, and the allow-list**

[showBusOn](qml/services/RoutingService.cpp#L984) is the new verb. It checks the graph's own edge set — not a cached snapshot — and refuses (through the existing `refused` toast) any bus that is not wired to that row. In the canvas, a **left-click on a video wire** makes that bus the picture on that output; right-click still cuts that one wire. The gesture sits in a `TapHandler`, not a widened `MouseArea`, so a press that turns into a drag (a port drag, a canvas drag) still falls through untouched. Wires now read honestly: solid is the bus on air, dashed and fainter is wired-but-not-showing ([RoutingScreen.qml:861](qml/screens/settings/RoutingScreen.qml#L861), [showWireAt](qml/screens/settings/RoutingScreen.qml#L1346)).

