Following the rule literally means a design's bus windows no longer paint on any output: an unwired row may not paint them (that's the rule), and a wired row shows that bus full-frame instead of inside the design rectangle. The Edit canvas and the app's own preview still draw windows, since they build ungated. If you want the *wired* row to also paint the window in its rectangle — i.e. design block on any row whose wires name that bus, rather than the full-frame feed — that's a different rule and a small change to which scene a wired row builds.

