The wire delegate had the same left-to-right assumption the ghost had: `control1X: x1 + bend`, `control2X: x2 - bend`, with `bend` from `|x2 - x1|`. That reads correctly only while `x1 < x2`, so it now normalises the ends exactly like the ghost does — `reversed: modelData.x2 < modelData.x1`, then `fromX/fromY` and `toX/toY`, with the handles placed to the outside of each end and the `PathCubic` anchored on `fromX/fromY`. Same formula, same numbers as `draggedWire`, so a wire and the ghost that created it are the same curve no matter which end the drag started from.

