Implementation:

```cpp
// The window's own box, after its fit (the MEDIA tab's Fit row, the same four
// choices a picture has). The engine cannot clip, so cover crops the SOURCE to
// the window's aspect and contain keeps the whole feed inside it; blur keeps the
// sharp feed contain-fitted (the softened backdrop is a preview effect — a
// per-frame 24px blur over a live feed would cost more than it shows).
rendering::Rect FitRectFor(const rendering::RgbaImage& img, const rendering::Rect& box,
                           const std::string& fit) {
    if (fit == "fill")
        return box;
    return ContainRectIn(img.width, img.height, box);
}
```

